  > Task :populateArtifactURLs
  I couldn't update `metadata/net.minidev/accessors-smart/index.json`. The Edit tool was denied because the session is in don't-ask mode, and I haven't tried to work around that. I need Edit permission, or your go-ahead to write the file another way.
  
  This is the content I would add to the `2.4.3` entry. It is the only change, and the existing `1.2` entry already uses the same source and documentation templates.
  
  ```json
  "source-code-url" : "https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/net/minidev/accessors-smart/$version$/accessors-smart-$version$-sources.jar",
  "repository-url" : "https://github.com/netplex/json-smart-v2",
  "test-code-url" : "https://github.com/netplex/json-smart-v2/tree/00955f7fb9705f4ad1c5f4956f2466344ebb2eae/accessors-smart/src/test",
  "documentation-url" : "https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/net/minidev/accessors-smart/$version$/accessors-smart-$version$-javadoc.jar",
  "description" : "accessors-smart provides an ASM-based helper for generating fast bean accessors for getter, setter, constructor, and field access operations. It is used by json-smart to reduce the overhead of Java reflection when mapping and converting object properties."
  ```
  
  - **Language:** The library isn't specific to Kotlin, Groovy or Scala, so the `language` field stays absent.
